---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Turtle Terrarium Guide: Aqua-Terrarium Setup | NS Reptiles"
  description="Turtle aqua-terrarium guide: dimensions, land-to-water ratio, filter, UVB and decor. What to know before you buy, from NS Reptiles in Novi Sad, Serbia."
  keywords="turtle terrarium, turtle aqua-terrarium, semi-aquatic turtle enclosure, turtle tank size, turtle UVB lamp, custom turtle terrarium Serbia"
  path="/en/guides/turtle-terrarium.html"
  image="/style/img/terrariums/ta-50x35x45x25-zuto-drvo-web.webp"
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle="Turtle Terrarium — Aqua-Terrarium Setup Guide | NS Reptiles"
  ogDescription="All about turtle aqua-terrariums: size, equipment, filter, UVB lamp and common mistakes. NS Reptiles, Novi Sad."
  translations={translationsFor("/en/guides/turtle-terrarium.html")}
  schema={schema}
>
<section class="page-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1>Turtle Terrarium</h1>
        <p>
          An aqua-terrarium — a glass home with a land and a water section — is the
          only right choice for semi-aquatic turtles. In this guide we go through the
          dimensions, equipment and setup step by step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <div class="wrap">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/en/terrariums.html">Terrariums</a></li>
          <li aria-current="page">Turtle Terrarium</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </nav>
<section class="animal-hero reveal">
      <div class="wrap">
        <img src="/style/img/terrariums/ta-50x35x45x25-zuto-drvo-web.webp" alt="Turtle aqua-terrarium with a land and a water section — NS Reptiles" width="1080" height="1080" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" class="animal-hero-img">
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">What is an aqua-terrarium</h2>

        <div class="animal-detail-grid">

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Land and water sections</h3>
            <p>
              An aqua-terrarium is a glass enclosure that combines a land section
              and a water section in one space. Turtles use the water section for
              swimming and hydration, and the land section for resting, basking
              under a heat lamp and laying eggs. Without one of the two sections,
              the housing conditions don't match the natural way of life of these
              animals.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Which species it is for</h3>
            <p>
              An aqua-terrarium is the right solution for semi-aquatic turtles that
              spend a significant part of their time in water. Tortoises, which live
              on dry ground and eat plants, don't need a water section — a classic
              terrarium with substrate and under-floor heating suits them. If you
              are not sure which type is right for you, feel free to contact us.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Custom builds</h3>
            <p>
              Every aqua-terrarium at NS Reptiles is handmade from glass, to your
              measurements and wishes. You can choose the dimensions, the finish
              color, the land-to-water ratio and the full equipment. We build
              terrariums to order — you choose the color, size and equipment. See our
              <a href="/en/custom-terrariums.html">custom terrarium builds page</a>
              or contact us directly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Ready-made models</h3>
            <p>
              Besides custom builds, we also offer ready-made aqua-terrariums in
              standard sizes — from a 50x35 cm up to a 100x45 cm footprint. All
              models are made of glass with a decorative film of your choice. You
              can see the full range on our
              <a href="/en/terrariums.html">terrariums page</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl" style="background: var(--bg);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">How big should an aqua-terrarium be</h2>

        <div class="proc">

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Minimum dimensions</h3>
              <p>
                For young turtles the minimum footprint is 50x35 cm, but keep in
                mind that turtles grow. Adults need 80x45 cm or more. We recommend
                buying an aqua-terrarium sized for the adult right away — that way
                you don't have to replace equipment as the animal grows.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Land-to-water ratio</h3>
              <p>
                The water section should cover 50 to 60% of the aqua-terrarium's
                total area. The land section is for resting and basking under the
                lamp, so it must be roomy enough for the animal to lie down freely.
                The water should be deep enough for the turtle to turn itself over
                without difficulty — usually twice the width of its shell.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Aqua-terrarium height</h3>
              <p>
                Height is not as critical as with terrariums for climbing species,
                but it must be enough to mount the lamp at a safe height above the
                land section. A minimum height of 40 cm is recommended for standard
                models.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">Essential equipment</h2>

        <div class="proc">

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Water filter</h3>
              <p>
                A filter is a must and it has to be powerful enough. Turtles produce
                significantly more waste than fish, so we recommend a filter with a
                capacity three to four times the actual water volume. Internal
                filters are practical for smaller aqua-terrariums, while external
                filters are a better choice for larger models. Rinse the filter
                sponge once a week.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>UVB lamp</h3>
              <p>
                UVB lighting is essential — without it the turtle cannot synthesize
                vitamin D3, which it needs to absorb calcium. A lamp with a 5 to 10%
                UVB rating, placed over the land section, is recommended. Replace
                the lamp every 12 months, because UVB output drops even before the
                lamp stops lighting up.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Heat lamp</h3>
              <p>
                A heat lamp is placed over the land section to create a warm basking
                zone. The temperature in the warm zone should be 30 to 35 degrees.
                The rest of the aqua-terrarium should be cooler, around 22 to 26
                degrees, so the animal can regulate its body temperature.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Water heater</h3>
              <p>
                The water temperature should be between 22 and 26 degrees. An
                aquarium heater with a thermostat keeps the temperature stable and
                prevents sudden changes that can harm the turtle's health. It goes
                in the water section, away from the spot where the turtle spends
                most of its time.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Ramp and land area</h3>
              <p>
                A ramp or shelf that lets the turtle climb out of the water onto the
                land section easily is a must. It has to be stable and have a rough
                surface so the turtle doesn't slip. The land section can be filled
                with a sandy substrate or left as glass covered with tiles —
                depending on the owner's preference and the turtle species.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl" style="background: var(--bg);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">How to set up an aqua-terrarium</h2>

        <div class="animal-detail-grid">

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Bottom of the water section</h3>
            <p>
              The bottom of the water section can be left bare (glass) or covered
              with coarse gravel larger in diameter than the turtle's shell. Fine
              sand and small gravel should be avoided because of the risk of
              swallowing. A bare bottom makes cleaning easier and reduces waste
              buildup.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Decorations</h3>
            <p>
              You can decorate the water section with stone decorations and lava
              rocks that are safe for the animals. Plastic plants add looks and
              hiding spots. Live aquatic plants are possible, but turtles will often
              eat or dig them up. All decorations must be stable — turtles are strong
              and knock over anything that is not well secured.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>3D background</h3>
            <p>
              A styrofoam or stone 3D background gives the aqua-terrarium a
              naturalistic look and adds extra surface for climbing and resting. At
              NS Reptiles we offer several types of 3D backgrounds — from classic
              stone patterns to decorative models. The background is glued in
              before filling with water.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="animal-fact reveal">
            <h3>Ambient lighting</h3>
            <p>
              Besides the UVB and heat lamps, you can add decorative LED lighting
              for a better look. LED strips along the edge of the lid or behind the
              background look nicer without significantly affecting temperature. A
              day/night cycle of 12 hours of light and 12 hours of darkness should
              be kept all year round.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">Common aqua-terrarium setup mistakes</h2>

        <div class="proc">

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>An aqua-terrarium that is too small</h3>
              <p>
                The most common mistake is buying a tank that is too small "until
                the turtle grows". Not enough space leads to stress, aggressive
                behavior and poorer health. Buy an aqua-terrarium sized for the
                adult size of your species right away.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>A filter that is not powerful enough</h3>
              <p>
                A filter whose capacity equals the water volume is not enough.
                Turtles are messy animals — the filter must be considerably more
                powerful than the minimum, and part of the water must be changed
                once a week regardless of how it looks.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Leaving out the UVB lamp</h3>
              <p>
                Without UVB lighting, the turtle will develop metabolic bone disease
                — a softening shell, deformities and serious health problems. A UVB
                lamp is not an optional extra but basic equipment. Replace it every
                12 months.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Cold water without a heater</h3>
              <p>
                Turtles are ectothermic animals — the ambient temperature directly
                affects their metabolism, digestion and immunity. Water colder than
                20 degrees slows the metabolism and raises the risk of disease. A
                heater with a thermostat is an easy way to avoid this.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>An unstable ramp</h3>
              <p>
                A ramp that moves or wobbles discourages turtles from climbing onto
                land. An animal that cannot bask normally under the lamp won't get
                enough heat, which affects its health in the long run. Make sure the
                ramp is firmly secured.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl" style="background: var(--bg);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="sec-title reveal">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        <div class="proc">

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>What is a turtle aqua-terrarium?</h3>
              <p>
                An aqua-terrarium is a combination of a terrarium and an aquarium
                that has both a land and a water section in one enclosure. It is
                ideal for semi-aquatic turtles that spend time both on land and in
                water.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Do you build custom aqua-terrariums?</h3>
              <p>
                Yes, we build aqua-terrariums to order — you can choose the size,
                finish color, land-to-water ratio and extra equipment.
                Contact us for a quote or visit our
                <a href="/en/custom-terrariums.html">custom terrarium builds page</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>What filter should I use for an aqua-terrarium?</h3>
              <p>
                We recommend a filter with a capacity three to four times the water
                volume. Internal filters suit smaller models, external filters suit
                models of 80x45 cm and larger. Regular partial water changes are a
                must regardless of the filter type.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="proc-step reveal">
            <div class="proc-num"></div>
            <div class="proc-body">
              <h3>Do tortoises need an aqua-terrarium?</h3>
              <p>
                No. Tortoises, which eat plants, live on dry ground and need a
                classic terrarium with substrate, under-floor heating and a UVB
                lamp. An aqua-terrarium is meant for semi-aquatic species. If you
                are not sure which species suits your conditions, feel free to
                ask us.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="usl-more">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="usl-more-head">
          <h2>More about <b>terrariums and services</b></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="usl-more-grid">
          <a class="usl-link" href="/en/terrariums.html">All terrariums
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="usl-link" href="/en/custom-terrariums.html">Custom terrarium builds
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="usl-link" href="/en/guides/turtle-aquarium.html">Aquatic turtle guide — aquarium
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="usl-link" href="/en/aquariums.html">Our aquariums
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="zcta">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Contact us <b>before you buy</b></h2>
        <p>
          We will help you choose the right size and equipment for your pet —
          no guesswork and no mistakes. We build aqua-terrariums to order.
        </p>
        <div class="zcta-btns">
          <a href="https://wa.me/381693301474?text=Hi%2C%20I%27m%20interested%20in%20a%20turtle%20aqua-terrarium" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn" style="background: #fff; color: var(--green-dark)" onclick="gtag('event', 'kontakt_click', {'metod': 'whatsapp_cta'})">WhatsApp</a>
          <a href="tel:+381693301474" class="btn btn-light" onclick="gtag('event', 'telefon_click', {'metod': 'poziv_cta'})">+381 69 330 1474</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


</Base>
